From bbbdbca3e4d9db4cf55b83c5f314a8f6d1334808 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vkd3d-crossover <noreply@vkd3d-crossover.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:12:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] chore(dev): add MTLBinaryArchive pipeline cache
 experiment

Problem: Compile hitches were attributed to Metal's implicit cache not being written for Wine processes.

Root cause: That premise was wrong: Metal's cache works under Wine (DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR/com.codeweavers.CrossOver.wineloader/com.apple.metal).

Fix: Utility/MVKBinaryArchive.h: per-program archive segments in ~/Library/Caches/MoltenVK/archives; render/compute/mesh pipelines and attachment variants try a fail-on-miss lookup first. Kept as an experiment only; candidate for removal.

Verified by: Deadlocked PRAGMATA SKETCHBOOK with a periodic save, MDB_MAP_FULL on large segments, and a hang loading a 21 MB segment; therefore off.

Off switch: off by default; MVK_BINARY_ARCHIVE=1 enables
---
 MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKPipeline.mm  |   7 +
 MoltenVK/MoltenVK/Utility/MVKBinaryArchive.h | 294 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 301 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 MoltenVK/MoltenVK/Utility/MVKBinaryArchive.h

